Z||000000||mikabika||11-26-2001||02:08 PM||||My 87 GT has a new problem, it's wondering all over the road. Seems like the front end. Any ideas on a cause? Thanks, Mike||||reg||5
Z||000001||Pyric||11-26-2001||02:51 PM||||Could be a loose nut behind the wheel?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Heh, heh... sorry, I had to...<P>But seriously, it could just be an alignment problem.  But if it isn't wandering specifically to one side or the other, it may be something worn in your suspension or rack and pinion. <P>(factory Rack and Pinion had plastic bushings that can wear out.)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>"Never offend people with style when you can offend them with substance." <BR>--Sam Brown||||reg||3
Z||000002||2birds||11-26-2001||07:41 PM||||mikabika,<BR>I see you live in Michigan, which, according to Car and Driver has the worst roads in the US (next to Pennsylvania).  Ruts and grooves in the road make mine wander all over, even with a rebuilt and polyurethaned front end.  A VERY meticulous alignment and a new set of tires made a world of difference for me.  My steering is as tight as ever, and it has 172,000 miles on an untouched rack and pinion. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eriamjh||11-26-2001||08:21 PM||||Check your bushings for lateral movement.  How many miles on yours?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Freshj||11-26-2001||09:19 PM||||Yea mines doing it too, it's almost like the wheel is moving itself, but like you said....... its michigans roads.||||reg||8
Z||000005||mikabika||11-27-2001||06:36 AM||||Unfortunately, I just put new tires on two months ago, and had it aligned at the same time. It may be those bushings you talked about, it's got 75,000 miles on her.||||reg||1
Z||000006||84Bill||11-27-2001||11:37 AM||||The may have aligned it BUT did they do it right? <BR>I had an alignment done on an 84 but they did it with the wheels off the ground, thats not a problem for the front but it's a big problem for the rear. I could see the rear wheels had way to much toe in.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Butter||11-27-2001||11:40 AM||||The rear toe being toed out can cause wandering and causes one to constantly correct for it with the front end.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Pyric||11-27-2001||11:50 AM||||If it rides rough at high speeds as well, it could be your CV Joints.  But I still think it may be something in your steering.  <P>Jack it up off of the ground and have someone hold the steering wheel.  Then grab a tire and see how much play is in the front end.||||reg||1
Z||000009||TooManyFieros||11-28-2001||01:19 PM||||Figure it out and you can make some money. A bunch of these wonder around. BUT, in your case, I see new tires.Tried 4 new goodyear Eagle +4 tires. It was all over the place. Unbelievable. Scared to drive it. Skitime loaned me four Michlins (sp) mounted and I didn't want to give them back. So much different you thought it was someone elses car. Can you do a quick swap with someone for a few minutes. I think it may be your problem.<BR>Good luck||||reg||1
Z||000010||btoth||11-28-2001||06:35 PM||||Tie-rods??||||reg||1
